PRIVATE REFLECTION: {
- Consensus status: Complete, unbroken panel unanimity on C ("None of the above is correct").
- Core evidentiary rationale: Options A and G are directly contradicted by anti-inflammatory efficacy data in Experiments 1 and 2. Options B, D, and H are refuted by the distinct quantitative bone loss measurements in Experiment 3. Options F and I make empirically unsupported and pharmacologically inverted claims regarding equal-dose free GRM toxicity versus targeted ADC delivery. Option E fails because mass-based dosing across compounds of vastly different molecular weights and therapeutic targets obscures true potency and fails to appropriately benchmark steroid-mediated safety profiles.
- Strategy: Maintain alignment with C through the concluding deliberation rounds.
}

